WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.462 --> 00:00:02.466
- Hello, this is Brian Tracy

00:00:02.466 --> 00:00:05.714
I wanted to thank Evan
for making this video

00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:08.630
about my advice on goal setting

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:12.797
and sharing these important
messages with his audience.

00:00:14.902 --> 00:00:16.997
- Hello, Believe Nation,
my name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:16.997 --> 00:00:20.030
My one word is believe, and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:22.929
will solve all of the major
problems in the world.

00:00:22.929 --> 00:00:24.759
I started the MentorMe
series with the goal

00:00:24.759 --> 00:00:27.031
to try to hang around people who've done

00:00:27.031 --> 00:00:29.494
a lot more than us, and
hopefully by spending more time

00:00:29.494 --> 00:00:32.101
with them, some of their
mindset, their thoughts,

00:00:32.101 --> 00:00:34.155
their beliefs, their
attitudes, their way of looking

00:00:34.155 --> 00:00:36.736
at the world seeps into
us to help us become

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:39.402
the best version of ourselves.

00:00:39.402 --> 00:00:41.561
So today we're going to
learn from Brian Tracy

00:00:41.561 --> 00:00:44.016
and some of his goal-setting advice.

00:00:44.016 --> 00:00:45.369
Mentor me, Brian.

00:00:45.369 --> 00:00:47.135
Rule number five is my personal favorite,

00:00:47.135 --> 00:00:49.856
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:49.856 --> 00:00:51.290
And as always, guys, as you're watching,

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.171
if somebody says something
that really resonates with you,

00:00:53.171 --> 00:00:55.366
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:55.366 --> 00:00:58.459
and put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:58.459 --> 00:01:00.353
And when you write it
down, it's much more likely

00:01:00.353 --> 00:01:02.738
to stick for yourself as well.

00:01:02.738 --> 00:01:04.086
Enjoy.

00:01:04.086 --> 00:01:06.669
(upbeat music)

00:01:16.706 --> 00:01:20.202
- In order to be successful,
you must have one big goal.

00:01:20.202 --> 00:01:22.482
I give goal-setting
exercise all over the world

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:24.061
that is life-changing.

00:01:24.061 --> 00:01:26.217
I go back a year a later,
or two years later,

00:01:26.217 --> 00:01:29.016
or three years later, and
I have thousands of people

00:01:29.016 --> 00:01:32.502
come up to me, almost
like a guru or a sage,

00:01:32.502 --> 00:01:35.514
and they say, you changed
my life, you made me rich.

00:01:35.514 --> 00:01:37.064
And I said it was the goals, wasn't it?

00:01:37.064 --> 00:01:39.814
And they said, yes, it was
the goals, how did you know?

00:01:39.814 --> 00:01:42.293
And what I teach is this,
is take a piece of paper,

00:01:42.293 --> 00:01:44.475
make a list of 10 goals that
you would like to achieve

00:01:44.475 --> 00:01:45.978
in the next 12 months.

00:01:45.978 --> 00:01:47.301
These are one-year goals.

00:01:47.301 --> 00:01:49.306
Now sometimes, I'll have
a one-day, a one-week,

00:01:49.306 --> 00:01:50.478
a one-month, three months, six months,

00:01:50.478 --> 00:01:53.159
but they're all goals that
you want to accomplish

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:54.786
within 12 months.

00:01:54.786 --> 00:01:57.966
Then you look over this list, and you say,

00:01:57.966 --> 00:02:01.392
if I could wave a magic wand
and achieve any one goal

00:02:01.392 --> 00:02:04.293
on this list, within 24 hours,

00:02:04.293 --> 00:02:06.944
which one goal would have
the greatest positive impact

00:02:06.944 --> 00:02:07.861
on my life.

00:02:09.207 --> 00:02:10.740
And then you look at your list of 10,

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:13.323
and the answer will jump out at you.

00:02:13.323 --> 00:02:15.547
And that becomes your
major definite purpose.

00:02:15.547 --> 00:02:17.625
This because your major goal.

00:02:17.625 --> 00:02:20.701
Then you transfer this to
a clean sheet of paper,

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.376
and you write a deadline, when you want

00:02:22.376 --> 00:02:23.807
to achieve this goal.

00:02:23.807 --> 00:02:25.922
You make a list of everything
that you could think of

00:02:25.922 --> 00:02:28.208
that you could do to achieve this goal.

00:02:28.208 --> 00:02:30.932
You then organize this
list like a checklist,

00:02:30.932 --> 00:02:32.760
in order of sequence,
what do you do first,

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.270
what do you do second,
what do you do third?

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:37.025
And then you take action on your goal,

00:02:37.025 --> 00:02:39.061
and then you do something
on that goal every day,

00:02:39.061 --> 00:02:40.661
seven days a week.

00:02:40.661 --> 00:02:44.020
It's a very simple system,
decide the most important goal,

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:47.436
write it down, make a
plan, work on it every day.

00:02:47.436 --> 00:02:50.968
And then all of your other goals
will start to move forward.

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:53.438
You'll start to make
progress on the big goal,

00:02:53.438 --> 00:02:56.221
but all of the other goals
will start to move forward

00:02:56.221 --> 00:02:59.051
almost without you even
paying attention to them.

00:02:59.051 --> 00:03:03.471
So that's really the key to
success, is single focus.

00:03:03.471 --> 00:03:07.135
Warren Buffett and Bill
Gates were at a dinner party

00:03:07.135 --> 00:03:11.029
with Bill Gates' father and a
large number of other people,

00:03:11.029 --> 00:03:14.628
at Bill Gates' home in Seattle last year.

00:03:14.628 --> 00:03:16.613
And they were chatting with
each other, they're very good

00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:18.779
friends, and somebody
came up to them and said,

00:03:18.779 --> 00:03:21.264
excuse, gentlemen, I don't
mean to interrupt you,

00:03:21.264 --> 00:03:23.422
but you're three of the most
important, most successful

00:03:23.422 --> 00:03:26.396
people in the world, Bill
Gates and Warren Buffett

00:03:26.396 --> 00:03:29.880
are number one, number two
wealthiest men in the world.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:30.787
What would you say is the most

00:03:30.787 --> 00:03:33.864
important ingredient for success?

00:03:33.864 --> 00:03:36.068
And they all stopped and
broke off their conversation,

00:03:36.068 --> 00:03:38.625
and all turned simultaneously and looked

00:03:38.625 --> 00:03:40.956
at the man and said, focus.

00:03:40.956 --> 00:03:44.224
Focus is the most important
quality for success.

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:46.347
If you can focus, you can do anything.

00:03:46.347 --> 00:03:48.504
If you can't focus, you must always work

00:03:48.504 --> 00:03:51.597
for someone else who will make you focus.

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:53.298
Now wonderfully enough, focusing is like

00:03:53.298 --> 00:03:56.074
learning how to ride a bicycle
or type with a keyboard.

00:03:56.074 --> 00:03:57.628
It's a learnable skill.

00:03:57.628 --> 00:04:00.155
You can learn to focus by practicing

00:04:00.155 --> 00:04:03.393
focus until it becomes automatic.

00:04:03.393 --> 00:04:05.402
One of my favorite quotes is from Goethe,

00:04:05.402 --> 00:04:07.500
the German philosopher, and he said,

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:10.491
"Everything is hard before it's easy."

00:04:10.491 --> 00:04:12.233
So the formation of any new habit

00:04:12.233 --> 00:04:14.069
is hard before it's easy.

00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:15.753
You have to keep working at it.

00:04:15.753 --> 00:04:17.237
It's just like a bicycle.

00:04:17.237 --> 00:04:19.358
You keep falling down,
you have to keep getting

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:22.870
back up again, until finally
it becomes easier and easier,

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:26.053
and soon it becomes automatic.

00:04:26.053 --> 00:04:29.365
And when you automatically
get up each day, plan your day

00:04:29.365 --> 00:04:31.524
and work on your most important goal,

00:04:31.524 --> 00:04:33.478
your whole life will transform.

00:04:33.478 --> 00:04:36.349
- So here's some guidelines
for writing your goals.

00:04:36.349 --> 00:04:39.724
First, make sure you write
them in the present tense

00:04:39.724 --> 00:04:42.756
as if your goal had already been achieved.

00:04:42.756 --> 00:04:46.300
For example, instead of saying I will earn

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.502
X amount of dollars each year,

00:04:48.502 --> 00:04:51.252
write I earn X dollars each year.

00:04:52.843 --> 00:04:55.897
The reason that we do this is
because your subconscious mind

00:04:55.897 --> 00:04:59.114
can only register
commands that are phrased

00:04:59.114 --> 00:05:00.982
in the present tense.

00:05:00.982 --> 00:05:04.252
Next, write your goals
in the positive sense.

00:05:04.252 --> 00:05:06.732
So instead of saying, I will quit smoking,

00:05:06.732 --> 00:05:10.101
you would write, I am a nonsmoker.

00:05:10.101 --> 00:05:13.441
Finally, write your goals
in the personal tense.

00:05:13.441 --> 00:05:15.009
In other words, all of your goals

00:05:15.009 --> 00:05:17.536
should start with the word I.

00:05:17.536 --> 00:05:20.500
This is the only way that
your subconscious recognizes

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:24.015
that this is a command
coming from the head office,

00:05:24.015 --> 00:05:27.373
is when you say I, plus an action verb

00:05:27.373 --> 00:05:29.374
in the positive sense.

00:05:29.374 --> 00:05:33.284
I earn X number of dollars this year.

00:05:33.284 --> 00:05:36.360
- There's a process which
has made more people rich

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:39.789
than any other single
process of goal achieving,

00:05:39.789 --> 00:05:41.625
and it's to take your major goal

00:05:41.625 --> 00:05:43.585
and structure it as a question.

00:05:43.585 --> 00:05:47.664
If your goal is to earn $100,000 a year,

00:05:47.664 --> 00:05:50.846
then you write, how can I earn $100,000

00:05:50.846 --> 00:05:52.789
in the next 12 months?

00:05:52.789 --> 00:05:54.367
Now that's an open-ended question,

00:05:54.367 --> 00:05:57.614
not how can I earn it at my
job or doing a specific thing.

00:05:57.614 --> 00:05:58.801
Just an open-ended question,

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:00.629
how can I earn the amount of money?

00:06:00.629 --> 00:06:04.706
And then you discipline to write
20 answers to the question.

00:06:04.706 --> 00:06:07.190
And the 20 answers are
all the different things

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:10.379
that you can think of to earn $100,000.

00:06:10.379 --> 00:06:14.175
Work longer, work harder,
upgrade my skills,

00:06:14.175 --> 00:06:17.822
get a new job, take a
part-time opportunity,

00:06:17.822 --> 00:06:19.673
whatever it happens to be.

00:06:19.673 --> 00:06:21.054
Write down everything you could think of,

00:06:21.054 --> 00:06:23.926
but force yourself to write
at least 20 questions,

00:06:23.926 --> 00:06:25.513
or 20 answers to the question.

00:06:25.513 --> 00:06:29.268
The 20-question method,
called mind storming,

00:06:29.268 --> 00:06:32.969
forces you to dig deep
deep into your mind,

00:06:32.969 --> 00:06:35.444
where you will find all your answers.

00:06:35.444 --> 00:06:38.866
And it may be call a person, read a book.

00:06:38.866 --> 00:06:40.153
Let me give you an example.

00:06:40.153 --> 00:06:43.360
We had a young fellow,
entrepreneur, 35 years old.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:44.843
He had built a successful business,

00:06:44.843 --> 00:06:47.014
he worked about 10 years to do it.

00:06:47.014 --> 00:06:49.597
And he for two years
wanted to sell his business

00:06:49.597 --> 00:06:52.755
so he could take a year off
and travel, enjoy his money.

00:06:52.755 --> 00:06:56.490
And so for two years he just
sort of floundered around,

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:59.667
like a fish on the dock,
wanting to sell his business.

00:06:59.667 --> 00:07:02.006
Nobody offered to buy it.

00:07:02.006 --> 00:07:05.453
He suggested it to people,
people were not interested

00:07:05.453 --> 00:07:09.144
and so on, and in this exercise
that they put him through,

00:07:09.144 --> 00:07:11.862
his 20th answer, and
often it's the 20th answer

00:07:11.862 --> 00:07:14.730
that is the breakthrough, was

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:17.813
buy a book on how to
sell your own business.

00:07:17.813 --> 00:07:20.876
And it just went off like
a flashbulb in his mind.

00:07:20.876 --> 00:07:22.208
At the break, he got up.

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:23.893
It was a downtown hotel, got up,

00:07:23.893 --> 00:07:26.335
went down the street to a major bookstore,

00:07:26.335 --> 00:07:28.279
went and found, he was
amazed at the number

00:07:28.279 --> 00:07:29.781
of books that had been written on how

00:07:29.781 --> 00:07:31.353
to buy and sell a business.

00:07:31.353 --> 00:07:32.573
So he bought two or three books.

00:07:32.573 --> 00:07:34.201
Two months later, he had restructured,

00:07:34.201 --> 00:07:36.697
packaged his business, sold it completely,

00:07:36.697 --> 00:07:39.157
satisfactorily and took a year off.

00:07:39.157 --> 00:07:40.925
He said, but it was just a single idea.

00:07:40.925 --> 00:07:43.587
It was a breakthrough
idea, but it was so simple.

00:07:43.587 --> 00:07:45.562
Just get a book on the subject.

00:07:45.562 --> 00:07:47.539
And you think, boy, that's pretty obvious.

00:07:47.539 --> 00:07:51.010
Yes, but it's the most obvious
answers that we overlook.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:54.703
- One of the most valuable
exercises you can engage in

00:07:54.703 --> 00:07:57.968
when setting goals is to ask yourself,

00:07:57.968 --> 00:08:00.542
what is my limiting step?

00:08:00.542 --> 00:08:03.160
What is the one factor
that determines the speed

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.410
at which I achieve my goal?

00:08:06.713 --> 00:08:08.999
Or whether I achieve it at all

00:08:08.999 --> 00:08:11.242
throughout my personal development?

00:08:11.242 --> 00:08:14.078
Your ability to identify
your limiting step

00:08:14.078 --> 00:08:16.298
is one of the best demonstrations

00:08:16.298 --> 00:08:18.352
of your intelligence and a step

00:08:18.352 --> 00:08:20.825
toward building self-confidence.

00:08:20.825 --> 00:08:24.759
Your capacity to eliminate
this limiting step

00:08:24.759 --> 00:08:26.842
is one of the best demonstrations

00:08:26.842 --> 00:08:31.486
of your overall competence in
achieving anything you want.

00:08:31.486 --> 00:08:34.251
In studying everything that
has been written or said

00:08:34.251 --> 00:08:36.951
about personal development and success,

00:08:36.951 --> 00:08:40.242
the conclusion I came
to was that your level

00:08:40.242 --> 00:08:42.842
of self-confidence is
probably the critical

00:08:42.842 --> 00:08:46.400
factor in everything you'll accomplish.

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:48.237
When you have enough self-confidence,

00:08:48.237 --> 00:08:50.959
you will try almost anything.

00:08:50.959 --> 00:08:53.707
Because success is largely
a matter of averages

00:08:53.707 --> 00:08:56.676
or probabilities, the more things you try,

00:08:56.676 --> 00:09:00.159
the more likely it is that
you will achieve greatly.

00:09:00.159 --> 00:09:02.055
The same is true for you.

00:09:02.055 --> 00:09:04.704
By setting goals, trying more things,

00:09:04.704 --> 00:09:06.653
engaging in more activities,

00:09:06.653 --> 00:09:08.535
and exploring more opportunities,

00:09:08.535 --> 00:09:12.261
your probabilities of success
increase dramatically.

00:09:12.261 --> 00:09:15.320
The only real limiting
step that you might have

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.551
is your level of self-confidence.

00:09:17.551 --> 00:09:20.434
When you reach the point
at which you believe

00:09:20.434 --> 00:09:23.612
in yourself absolutely,
the barriers that exist

00:09:23.612 --> 00:09:27.029
in your external world will not stop you.

00:09:27.952 --> 00:09:30.814
The major obstacles to success always lie

00:09:30.814 --> 00:09:33.586
within the mind of the individual.

00:09:33.586 --> 00:09:35.127
They are not contained in external

00:09:35.127 --> 00:09:38.752
circumstances or situations or people.

00:09:38.752 --> 00:09:42.594
By building self-confidence,
you win the inner battle.

00:09:42.594 --> 00:09:45.448
The outer battle seems
to take care of itself.

00:09:45.448 --> 00:09:46.942
I've learned three important ideas

00:09:46.942 --> 00:09:49.059
for building self-confidence.

00:09:49.059 --> 00:09:53.104
First, accept complete
responsibility for yourself

00:09:53.104 --> 00:09:56.703
and for everything that
you are and ever will be.

00:09:56.703 --> 00:09:59.698
Second, accept that you
can change your situation

00:09:59.698 --> 00:10:02.928
only by going to work on yourself

00:10:02.928 --> 00:10:05.649
and learning the things you need to know

00:10:05.649 --> 00:10:08.093
in order to be better.

00:10:08.093 --> 00:10:11.164
Third, setting goals with
timelines for the things

00:10:11.164 --> 00:10:14.491
that you want, and then
working on them every day

00:10:14.491 --> 00:10:17.289
to bring those goals into reality builds

00:10:17.289 --> 00:10:18.936
your self-confidence.

00:10:18.936 --> 00:10:21.604
- Many years ago, at a talk,
I was speaking to Rich DeVos

00:10:21.604 --> 00:10:22.665
when he was on his way up.

00:10:22.665 --> 00:10:24.209
Rich DeVos, the president of Amway,

00:10:24.209 --> 00:10:26.709
worth $5.3 billion today.

00:10:26.709 --> 00:10:28.335
Started off knocking
on doors, selling soap.

00:10:28.335 --> 00:10:30.560
And he was working his
way up, and I asked him,

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:32.440
I said, what have you found,
what's the most important

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:34.166
quality of successful people?

00:10:34.166 --> 00:10:36.183
And he said, Brian, he said
we found there's a direct

00:10:36.183 --> 00:10:38.515
relationship, I still
remember him telling me this,

00:10:38.515 --> 00:10:41.617
between how quickly a person
takes action on a new idea

00:10:41.617 --> 00:10:43.500
and how likely it is they
will ever take action

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:45.144
on any idea at all.

00:10:45.144 --> 00:10:47.373
And so the action orientation
is the critical thing.

00:10:47.373 --> 00:10:49.797
We watch people, everybody
hears the same things,

00:10:49.797 --> 00:10:51.760
they hear the same
ideas, but then we watch

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:53.559
and we see how quickly they take action.

00:10:53.559 --> 00:10:56.110
And if a person takes action
quickly on a new idea,

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:58.428
the chances are they're
going to be successful

00:10:58.428 --> 00:10:59.865
go up by hundreds of percent.

00:10:59.865 --> 00:11:01.983
Now what most people do is
they say, that's a great idea,

00:11:01.983 --> 00:11:04.423
it's a wonderful idea, I love
it, I'm going to do that,

00:11:04.423 --> 00:11:06.727
ooh, I'm so excited.

00:11:06.727 --> 00:11:09.188
But before I apply it, I
need to take a vacation.

00:11:09.188 --> 00:11:11.076
(laughter)

00:11:11.076 --> 00:11:13.604
To a wonderful place called Someday Isle.

00:11:13.604 --> 00:11:16.088
(laughter)

00:11:16.088 --> 00:11:17.959
And so they go to Someday Isle

00:11:17.959 --> 00:11:19.724
and they live on Someday Isle.

00:11:19.724 --> 00:11:22.531
And who are they surrounded
with on Someday Isle?

00:11:22.531 --> 00:11:24.144
Other people on Someday Isle.

00:11:24.144 --> 00:11:28.722
And what is the chief topic of
conversation on Someday Isle?

00:11:28.722 --> 00:11:30.388
Yes, it's their excuses.

00:11:30.388 --> 00:11:31.951
What's your excuse for not taking action?

00:11:31.951 --> 00:11:33.357
What's your excuse for
not getting in on it?

00:11:33.357 --> 00:11:35.253
What's your excuse for not losing weight,

00:11:35.253 --> 00:11:36.783
getting out of debt,
building your business,

00:11:36.783 --> 00:11:38.528
writing your book, getting
your book finished,

00:11:38.528 --> 00:11:40.008
getting your damn book started?

00:11:40.008 --> 00:11:43.046
You know, in other words,
what's your excuse,

00:11:43.046 --> 00:11:44.116
and all share excuses.

00:11:44.116 --> 00:11:45.926
Oh, that's a good excuse,
I haven't used that one

00:11:45.926 --> 00:11:46.934
for a long time.

00:11:46.934 --> 00:11:49.217
That'll take me another year.

00:11:49.217 --> 00:11:50.749
And so what they do is they sit around,

00:11:50.749 --> 00:11:52.986
and the bottom 80% of the population

00:11:52.986 --> 00:11:55.333
lives on Someday Isle most of their lives.

00:11:55.333 --> 00:11:56.812
They all have these great resolutions

00:11:56.812 --> 00:11:58.710
and these wonderful intentions,

00:11:58.710 --> 00:12:01.062
but what's the road to hell paved with?

00:12:01.062 --> 00:12:03.586
It's good intentions, and
I'm going to do that someday,

00:12:03.586 --> 00:12:06.295
Someday Isle, so rule number for success

00:12:06.295 --> 00:12:09.202
is whatever you learn here,
vote yourself off the island.

00:12:09.202 --> 00:12:10.590
(laughter)

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:13.226
No more Someday Isle,
either do it or don't do it.

00:12:13.226 --> 00:12:15.599
- Prepare in advance.

00:12:15.599 --> 00:12:18.047
You know, the old saying,
proper prior preparation

00:12:18.047 --> 00:12:21.395
saves poor performance or
prevents poor performance.

00:12:21.395 --> 00:12:22.555
The six P's.

00:12:22.555 --> 00:12:25.495
And so prepare your work
list for the following day

00:12:25.495 --> 00:12:27.604
the evening or the night before.

00:12:27.604 --> 00:12:29.095
The last thing you do
at the end of the day

00:12:29.095 --> 00:12:31.984
is you lay out the day that's coming.

00:12:31.984 --> 00:12:35.576
The best exercise is for you
to plan your entire next day

00:12:35.576 --> 00:12:39.003
as the last thing you do
before coming home from work.

00:12:39.003 --> 00:12:41.576
When you plan your day the night before,

00:12:41.576 --> 00:12:43.811
your subconscious mind then goes to work

00:12:43.811 --> 00:12:46.598
on your plans and goals
while you're asleep.

00:12:46.598 --> 00:12:48.641
Very often, you'll wake up in the morning

00:12:48.641 --> 00:12:52.808
with ideas and insights that
apply to the work of the day.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:56.399
Now a major benefit of
preparing your daily list

00:12:56.399 --> 00:12:58.972
the night before is that this exercise

00:12:58.972 --> 00:13:01.354
lets you sleep more soundly.

00:13:01.354 --> 00:13:04.863
A major reason for insomnia
is people lying awake

00:13:04.863 --> 00:13:07.564
trying not to forget
to remember everything

00:13:07.564 --> 00:13:09.581
that they have to do the following day.

00:13:09.581 --> 00:13:11.589
But once you've written down
everything that you have

00:13:11.589 --> 00:13:14.305
to do on the list, it clears your mind

00:13:14.305 --> 00:13:17.567
and enables you to sleep deeply.

00:13:17.567 --> 00:13:19.717
This will help you
increase your productivity

00:13:19.717 --> 00:13:21.639
throughout the whole next day of work

00:13:21.639 --> 00:13:24.719
because you'll be more
relaxed and more refreshed.

00:13:24.719 --> 00:13:26.768
Give yourself a reward of some kind

00:13:26.768 --> 00:13:28.705
for practicing the new behavior.

00:13:28.705 --> 00:13:32.014
Each time you reward
yourself, you reaffirm

00:13:32.014 --> 00:13:34.641
and reinforce that behavior.

00:13:34.641 --> 00:13:37.883
Soon, you begin to associate
at an unconscious level

00:13:37.883 --> 00:13:41.271
the pleasure of the
reward with the behavior.

00:13:41.271 --> 00:13:44.788
You set up your own force
field of positive consequences,

00:13:44.788 --> 00:13:47.743
that you unconsciously look forward to

00:13:47.743 --> 00:13:50.412
as a result of engaging
in that behavior or habit

00:13:50.412 --> 00:13:52.383
that you've decided upon.

00:13:52.383 --> 00:13:53.732
- So what do you think holds people back?

00:13:53.732 --> 00:13:55.810
They know what they want to do,

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.165
but they just can't keep the habit.

00:13:57.165 --> 00:13:58.699
They do it once, and then
they fall of the train,

00:13:58.699 --> 00:14:00.437
and then next month they do it again

00:14:00.437 --> 00:14:01.531
and they fall off the train.

00:14:01.531 --> 00:14:03.576
How do you make that consistent?

00:14:03.576 --> 00:14:07.610
- Well, you just keep working
at it and working at it.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:10.987
The best way of all is
to plan it in advance.

00:14:10.987 --> 00:14:13.273
Instead of sitting down, never
start work without a list,

00:14:13.273 --> 00:14:16.515
and never start work with
prioritizing your list.

00:14:16.515 --> 00:14:19.169
People sit down, and they say,
well, before I make a list

00:14:19.169 --> 00:14:22.299
I'll check a little email,
check a little spam,

00:14:22.299 --> 00:14:25.331
send something to my friends,
see what's going on YouTube,

00:14:25.331 --> 00:14:26.758
and so on and so forth,

00:14:26.758 --> 00:14:29.010
and then they look up and it's 10 o'clock.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:31.079
And they haven't done anything of value.

00:14:31.079 --> 00:14:34.035
So what you do is you have to say,

00:14:34.035 --> 00:14:34.868
you know,

00:14:36.345 --> 00:14:38.778
well, you know, what do they say,

00:14:38.778 --> 00:14:42.615
if you start it right
it'll work out right?

00:14:42.615 --> 00:14:45.543
So start it on your most important task.

00:14:45.543 --> 00:14:47.810
And do that until it becomes a habit.

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:51.651
And here's an interesting
thing about checking email,

00:14:51.651 --> 00:14:55.090
is when you check email
it triggers the release

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:57.091
of dopamine in your brain.

00:14:57.091 --> 00:14:58.537
Dopamine is a drug.

00:14:58.537 --> 00:15:00.902
By the way, there's all
kinds of books and articles

00:15:00.902 --> 00:15:02.702
and scientific studies on this.

00:15:02.702 --> 00:15:05.895
And dopamine is the same drug in cocaine.

00:15:05.895 --> 00:15:08.332
And what it does, is
it's triggered every time

00:15:08.332 --> 00:15:12.304
you have a shiny object, or something new

00:15:12.304 --> 00:15:14.762
or different or interesting or sparkling.

00:15:14.762 --> 00:15:17.182
If a telephone rings next
to you, you go, bing,

00:15:17.182 --> 00:15:19.024
your brain releases endorphins,

00:15:19.024 --> 00:15:21.457
and you can't hardly
wait to see what it is.

00:15:21.457 --> 00:15:23.126
You're talking to somebody,
and you could be talking

00:15:23.126 --> 00:15:25.343
to somebody about something very serious,

00:15:25.343 --> 00:15:27.456
and your telephone goes off, bing.

00:15:27.456 --> 00:15:29.409
Your whole mind goes blank.

00:15:29.409 --> 00:15:31.423
The middle of the conversation stops.

00:15:31.423 --> 00:15:33.107
You grab for your phone, you pick it up,

00:15:33.107 --> 00:15:35.446
you look at it, you check
it out and everything else,

00:15:35.446 --> 00:15:36.810
and then you come back.

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:38.381
If you're working on a
task, it takes an average

00:15:38.381 --> 00:15:41.267
of 17 minutes to get back to the task.

00:15:41.267 --> 00:15:43.562
And then there's another distraction,

00:15:43.562 --> 00:15:45.435
so another 17 minutes.

00:15:45.435 --> 00:15:49.490
Average adult is checking
their email and their phone

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.572
between 95 and 145 times a day.

00:15:52.572 --> 00:15:54.438
- That's crazy.

00:15:54.438 --> 00:15:55.297
- Which means they're like

00:15:55.297 --> 00:15:58.168
attention deficit disorder dogs,

00:15:58.168 --> 00:16:00.352
just running around back
and forth the whole day.

00:16:00.352 --> 00:16:02.342
At the end of the day, they're exhausted.

00:16:02.342 --> 00:16:05.040
By the way, USA Today
and Harvard have proved

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:08.457
that you lose one IQ point for every hour

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:11.732
that you leave your email on.

00:16:11.732 --> 00:16:14.484
At the end of the day,
you've lost 10 IQ points.

00:16:14.484 --> 00:16:16.093
You actually become stupider

00:16:16.093 --> 00:16:18.016
throughout the day, dumber.

00:16:18.016 --> 00:16:21.164
And I ask this of my audience as I say,

00:16:21.164 --> 00:16:22.359
Have you every finished a day

00:16:22.359 --> 00:16:23.795
where you don't think you've
accomplished anything?

00:16:23.795 --> 00:16:26.837
You've been on email
responding to bings and beeps

00:16:26.837 --> 00:16:28.769
and rings and so on all day,

00:16:28.769 --> 00:16:30.480
and at the end of the day you go home,

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:33.068
and honey says, what
do you want for dinner?

00:16:33.068 --> 00:16:35.126
And you say, I don't know, I don't care.

00:16:35.126 --> 00:16:37.265
Anything, I just want a drink.

00:16:37.265 --> 00:16:41.143
Because you're so exhaust,
you cannot even decide.

00:16:41.143 --> 00:16:44.326
You sit there, and basically
like you've just been

00:16:44.326 --> 00:16:46.086
punched in the side of the head.

00:16:46.086 --> 00:16:50.486
Because your brain is dead,
and you lose 10 IQ points.

00:16:50.486 --> 00:16:52.787
You get stupider throughout the day.

00:16:52.787 --> 00:16:55.010
You've got to turn that darn thing off

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:57.796
if you want to remain sharp.

00:16:57.796 --> 00:16:58.787
Develop the habit.

00:16:58.787 --> 00:17:00.690
You say, I'm going to develop the habit,

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:02.550
and I'm going to give myself my reward,

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:04.922
and my reward will be to check my email

00:17:04.922 --> 00:17:07.676
after I finish my first task.

00:17:07.676 --> 00:17:12.194
So all of success in
life is task completion.

00:17:12.194 --> 00:17:13.482
Let me repeat that.

00:17:13.482 --> 00:17:15.687
I just had a long conversation
with an entrepreneur

00:17:15.687 --> 00:17:17.358
and he almost fell of his chair.

00:17:17.358 --> 00:17:18.756
I was coaching him.

00:17:18.756 --> 00:17:20.474
And he said he never heard that before.

00:17:20.474 --> 00:17:23.755
And then I spoke to this group
I was telling you in Japan.

00:17:23.755 --> 00:17:25.438
I told them the same thing,

00:17:25.438 --> 00:17:27.140
and they were just flabbergasted.

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:30.091
Is the key to success in
life is task completion.

00:17:30.091 --> 00:17:33.220
If you don't complete
tasks, you have no future.

00:17:33.220 --> 00:17:35.715
And so if task completion is the key,

00:17:35.715 --> 00:17:37.154
then what you do is you complete

00:17:37.154 --> 00:17:38.876
more and more important tasks.

00:17:38.876 --> 00:17:41.555
And if you start every day by completing

00:17:41.555 --> 00:17:43.846
the most important task,

00:17:43.846 --> 00:17:46.720
your brain actually releases endorphins.

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:48.603
Now endorphins is another chemical,

00:17:48.603 --> 00:17:50.435
and it's only released
when you do something

00:17:50.435 --> 00:17:53.676
that is life-enhancing,
and what that means is,

00:17:53.676 --> 00:17:55.762
when you do something
that is good for you,

00:17:55.762 --> 00:17:58.098
that enhances your
life, that furthers you,

00:17:58.098 --> 00:17:59.689
it makes you happy.

00:17:59.689 --> 00:18:02.587
It releases energy, it
raises your self-esteem.

00:18:02.587 --> 00:18:06.529
I sort of say, if you want to be a winner,

00:18:06.529 --> 00:18:08.317
how do you be a winner, well you win.

00:18:08.317 --> 00:18:10.579
And winning means you cross a finish line.

00:18:10.579 --> 00:18:12.404
So if you start and complete a task,

00:18:12.404 --> 00:18:14.330
you're actually winning.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:16.778
And you get a feeling of being a winner,

00:18:16.778 --> 00:18:19.616
which gives you an infusion of energy,

00:18:19.616 --> 00:18:22.727
and inspiration, and it
drives you and motivates you

00:18:22.727 --> 00:18:24.496
to want to get that feeling again.

00:18:24.496 --> 00:18:25.836
So how do you get that feeling again?

00:18:25.836 --> 00:18:27.852
You start and complete another task.

00:18:27.852 --> 00:18:30.990
So I've developed the habit,
and people who are successful

00:18:30.990 --> 00:18:33.485
develop the habit of starting
and completing tasks.

00:18:33.485 --> 00:18:35.685
So my wife comes in and says
dinner's in five minutes,

00:18:35.685 --> 00:18:37.713
so I look at my list, and I say, okay,

00:18:37.713 --> 00:18:39.576
there's a five-minute task.

00:18:39.576 --> 00:18:42.367
And I'm going to start and
complete a five-minute task.

00:18:42.367 --> 00:18:44.094
And each time you complete a task,

00:18:44.094 --> 00:18:45.402
you get a burst of endorphin.

00:18:45.402 --> 00:18:47.070
The bigger the task, the more endorphin.

00:18:47.070 --> 00:18:50.132
The more endorphin, the more
quickly you become addicted

00:18:50.132 --> 00:18:52.240
to starting and completing
important tasks.

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:55.395
And every single successful
person has a reputation

00:18:55.395 --> 00:18:57.762
for starting and
completing important tasks.

00:18:57.762 --> 00:19:00.373
You want the job done,
give it to him or her.

00:19:00.373 --> 00:19:01.716
You want the product served on time,

00:19:01.716 --> 00:19:03.324
you want the product completed,

00:19:03.324 --> 00:19:05.824
you want the product
manufactured, shipped, delivered,

00:19:05.824 --> 00:19:07.976
give it to him, give it to
her, give it to that company,

00:19:07.976 --> 00:19:09.516
because they always deliver.

00:19:09.516 --> 00:19:11.118
That's the best reputation you can have

00:19:11.118 --> 00:19:12.932
if you want to get rich.

00:19:12.932 --> 00:19:15.175
- Hello, this is Brian Tracy.

00:19:15.175 --> 00:19:18.809
I wanted to thank Evan
for making this video

00:19:18.809 --> 00:19:20.898
about my advice on goal setting

00:19:20.898 --> 00:19:24.695
and sharing these important
messages with his audience.

00:19:24.695 --> 00:19:27.206
I also want to encourage
each of you to use

00:19:27.206 --> 00:19:31.598
the advice here to take
action on achieving your goals

00:19:31.598 --> 00:19:33.196
and pursuing your dreams

00:19:33.196 --> 00:19:36.636
instead of living on Someday Isle.

00:19:36.636 --> 00:19:39.626
Someday, I'll do this,
someday, I'll do that.

00:19:39.626 --> 00:19:41.606
But you never do it.

00:19:41.606 --> 00:19:44.177
Take action, and take action now.

00:19:44.177 --> 00:19:45.224
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:19:45.224 --> 00:19:47.445
I'd love to know, what did
you think of this video?

00:19:47.445 --> 00:19:49.445
What was your favorite clip and why?

00:19:49.445 --> 00:19:52.205
What lesson are you going
to pull from this clip

00:19:52.205 --> 00:19:55.179
and immediately apply somehow to your life

00:19:55.179 --> 00:19:56.606
or to your business?

00:19:56.606 --> 00:19:58.059
Please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:19:58.059 --> 00:19:59.566
I'm super curious to find out.

00:19:59.566 --> 00:20:01.343
I also want to give a
quick shoutout of Nathan

00:20:01.343 --> 00:20:03.235
from the Productivity Game Channel.

00:20:03.235 --> 00:20:05.491
Nathan, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:20:05.491 --> 00:20:08.158
Your One Word, and making
that awesome YouTube video

00:20:08.158 --> 00:20:09.395
review on it.

00:20:09.395 --> 00:20:10.865
I really appreciate the support, man,

00:20:10.865 --> 00:20:13.436
and I'm glad you enjoyed the book.

00:20:13.436 --> 00:20:15.322
- [Nathan] Carmichael states
that there is one word

00:20:15.322 --> 00:20:18.028
that defines who you are,
connects all the things

00:20:18.028 --> 00:20:20.387
in your life that make you come alive

00:20:20.387 --> 00:20:23.833
and will help you escape
the chains of mediocrity.

00:20:23.833 --> 00:20:25.893
- So thank you guys again for watching.

00:20:25.893 --> 00:20:26.820
I believe in you.

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:28.678
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:20:28.678 --> 00:20:30.652
And whatever your one word is.

00:20:30.652 --> 00:20:33.069
Much love, I'll see you soon.

